																		The Macguffin
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fireknight" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5930130); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5930130&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609873344" alt="Fireknight" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5930130)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fireknight" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5930130); return false;" >Fireknight</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607663343 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Dec 2020 05:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842006">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An old locket, when someone touches it they begin on a journey to face some evil person or organization. They’ll defeat the villain in some epic showdown and everyone lives happily ever after.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Yay!&nbsp;Happily&nbsp;ever&nbsp;after!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Yeah,&nbsp;of&nbsp;course&nbsp;there’s&nbsp;more</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>There’s a few catches. First, someone always touches the locket, it’s destiny. That’s not to say that this is uncontainable, but the journeys need to be managed instead of prevented. Which is especially difficult due to catch two, the Foundation meets all the requirements to be a villain. So their top priority is obviously making sure they never get selected as a target. But then comes in catch three, because the obvious containment method is to simply send someone on a scripted adventure. But when you script the adventure, you become the villain. I don’t know if you’ve caught on by now but this article is all about the Foundation trying to contain fate, which is completely illogical. But the thing is, they do it.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The meat of the story will be told through test logs where the Foundation will experiment with different containment procedures. For instance, what happens if you have someone touch the locket, then you terminate them? (Spoiler alert, the same thing that happens when the protagonist of a book is facing down a firing squad, it doesn’t end well for the firing squad). In the end, they contain it by having an independent task force act as the villains. The task force doesn’t know they’re meant to be villains, they know that they have one objective, “kill anyone who touches the locket”. They also know that they keep failing. Since the task force isn’t directly controlled by the Foundation, the Foundation is safe from becoming the villains.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Two things. One, fate isn’t that common of a system to show up in SCPs. The second one I haven’t mentioned yet, but this is actually a completely non lethal SCP. The person affected by the locket is both incapable of dying and incapable of killing people. That’s not to say it’s not dangerous though. I’m considering adding a discovery log where someone with this locket collapses a corporation that was exploiting people, but at the same time puts millions of people out of work.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I want to know if you think this is too many ideas in one or if it ties together well. MAJOR CHANGES BELOW</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

