<p>Thanks for the critique! About what defines evil. It’s not about what is actually evil. In fact, I’m not planning on using the words “evil” or “villain” anywhere in the article. It’s just that there are some consistent traits across all people and organizations that the locket defeats. The Foundation has noticed that they meet these traits. You seem to be suggesting switching the focus to moral questioning. It’s a neat idea, I just don’t know where I’d go with it. Right now I’m mostly focusing on the containment of this. While an overhaul’s fine if necessary I’m not really sure what I’d write about with that idea. I’ll think about it though. Thanks again, it’s always good to hear another perspective after thinking about an idea for a while.</p>

