<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Placeholder! Got summoned via PM to take a look-see. Will crit in a bit.</span></p>
<p>Alright, here’s my take.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First off, I do like the unique take on containment this concept focuses on. If the Foundation is anything, it’s creative and cautious. Your idea seems to meet both of those, though I’m a bit iffy on the logic vis a vis why the task force needs to be kept in the dark.</p>
<p>Honestly, at this point, my main concern is that there’s missed opportunity here. The SCP universe isn’t exactly a canon with a lot of conventional moral dichotomies and heroes. Introducing an artifact that can both railroad Foundation attempts to suppress it and bring the ethical choices of the organization into question is a big idea that feels rather wasted on containment squabbles</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
If you respond to this comment and would like me to see it, please send me a Wikidot PM, as I will not be notified otherwise.
