														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857897">
									

<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">MAJOR CHANGES</span></p>
<p>Well then, I know it’s been a while but I think I know what to do.</p>
<p>Earlier I said that the Foundation couldn’t aim this artifact. I’m changing that, they did weaponize it, for a time. The main thing I’m changing is the way it targets a villain. Instead of the locket having its own sense of right and wrong it targets someone the holder views as evil. The thing is, it targets anyone nearby that is evil enough, that’s always been how it works I’m just making it clear.</p>
<p>What I’m planning on adding is a program where the Foundation uses the locket to defeat some small GOIs. It works, for a time. Then during one attempt, the holder of the locket turns around and proceeds to attack the Foundation. Causing serious damage and even unseating a site administrator. After being interviewed the holder confesses that they’d been questioning the morality of the Foundation for some time but had never thought of doing anything about it. That’s when the Foundation realizes that no amount of psychology or loyalty tests can tell if someone truly, in their heart of hearts, believes the Foundation is good. So they discontinue the program.</p>

							</div>

								
					
