														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4862296">
									

<p>I do like the change to make the locket somewhat utile to the Foundation. I would, however, like some clarification regarding this part:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After being interviewed the holder confesses that they’d been questioning the morality of the Foundation for some time but had never thought of doing anything about it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What about the Foundation's practices would be called into question here? I know that might seem like a silly question, but every author tends to have different 'headcanons' regarding what the Foundation makes public knowledge among its staff. Would this be in regards to the containment procedures of specific anomalies, or the overarching philosophy of &quot;Contain First, Ask Questions Later&quot;?</p>
<p>As a side point, does this mean that the locket is no longer connected to 'destiny' as a supreme force? That might change things as well.</p>

							</div>

								
