			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863066">
									

<p>I’d say the agent would be questioning the way The Foundation contains humanoid anomalies and the way it treats d-class. Both of which are fairly low clearance but also can be moral grey areas.</p>
<p>As for destiny, I’ll admit I’ve had a fairly flimsy definition. The idea of the locket is that it unlocks people’s personal destinies. There’s also the overarching force of destiny that forces people to touch it. Personal destinies are things that people are always meant to do. They may not know on the beforehand, but they always feel very satisfied when they’re done.</p>

